From 582d9dc80e9055387163119f17f1db040ff3bc4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:39:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(drilling): Auto reads the depth in material; add the
 Deep cycle choice

Auto chose the cycle by R plane - bottom, so the air above a hole's mouth
counted as depth: a 3.5 mm spot under a 5 mm gap posted G73 with an
18 mm peck step. Auto now reads the depth from the mouth (or a lower R
plane) in the axial cycle, the radial cycle (from d = 0, not the R
standoff) and the setup sheet, as the drill page note already did. The
plunge still starts at the R plane.

A new cycle choice Deep ("deep", "Deep peck (full retract)") posts the
full-retract peck (G83) on any hole. It is appended to the combo and the
digest, so older operations keep their indices and stamps. The cross-hole
cycle maps it before its unreachable arm.

Fixes #2443

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
