+        // #2443: full-retract pecking, appended so older indices stay.
+        10 => C::Deep,
         _ => C::Auto,
     }
 }
diff --git a/docs/decisions/2443-drill-auto-depth.md b/docs/decisions/2443-drill-auto-depth.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..4b6eb10ed4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/2443-drill-auto-depth.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+## #2443 - Drill Auto reads the depth in material; the Deep cycle choice
+
+**Decided.**
+
+- Auto measures a hole's depth from its mouth (`Hole::entry_z`), or from
+  the R plane when the R plane stands lower. It never counts the air
+  between a high R plane and the mouth. The same reading is in the axial
+  cycle (`drilling::cycle`), the radial cycle (`drilling::cross`, depth
+  from d = 0, not from the R standoff) and the setup sheet. The drill page
+  note already read `entry_z - floor_z`, so generation now agrees with it.
+- A new cycle choice `Deep` (`"deep"` in the project file and MCP,
+  "Deep peck (full retract)" in the combo) resolves to the existing
+  `CycleKind::Deep`, which every canned-cycle post writes as `G83`.
+- `list_operation_types` already lists the cycle words (#3449). The test
+  now also asks for `deep`.
+
+**Why.** A 3.5 mm spot under a 5 mm air gap read as 8.5 mm deep and posted
+a `G73` with a peck step longer than the hole. The cycle choice must follow
+the material that the drill cuts. A user with a deep or gummy hole had no
+way to ask for full retracts.
+
+**The plunge still starts at the R plane.** Only the choice of cycle reads
+the mouth. The feed moves, the peck steps and the posted R word do not
+change.
+
+**Dropped.**
+
+- Measure from the stock top over the hole. The mouth is what the hole
+  list stores, and the R-plane law (#91) already keeps the rapid out of
+  uncut stock.
+- Put `Deep` at the next free index of the enum in the middle of the combo.
+  It is appended (index 10), so the combo indices and the digest bytes of
+  older operations do not change.
+
+**Effect on programs.** A hole whose R plane is more than one diameter
+above its mouth can change from `G73` to `G81`, or from `G83` to `G73`,
+under Auto. A program that does not use Auto, and a hole whose R plane is
+at its mouth, posts byte-identical.
+
+**Cost to change later.** One expression in three readers, and one enum
+word.
diff --git a/site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md b/site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md
index c4f6f4ab52..c79d08fa4e 100644
--- a/site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md
+++ b/site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md
@@ -838,12 +838,19 @@ starts empty and refuses to generate until it has holes.
 |---|---|---|
 | Heights | R plane (feed starts here) | model top + 0 |
 | Heights | Bottom Z | each hole's own floor; **Override the hole floors** to set one |
-| Passes | Cycle | Auto: the tool decides (a tap taps, a boring bar bores, a drill chooses by depth against diameter); or Spot, Drill, Peck, Tap (rigid), Bore, Back bore, Tap (floating holder) |
+| Passes | Cycle | Auto: the tool decides (a tap taps, a boring bar bores, a drill chooses by the depth in material against its diameter); or Spot, Drill, Peck, Tap (rigid), Bore, Back bore, Tap (floating holder), Ream, Fine bore, Deep peck (full retract) |
 | Passes | Peck depth | Auto (by the cycle) |
 | Passes | Dwell at bottom | 0 s |
 
 Tools: drill, tap or boring bar.
 
+Auto measures each hole's depth from its mouth, not from the R plane. The
+air between the R plane and the hole does not count. A drill takes the
+Drill cycle (`G81`) to one diameter of material, the chip-break Peck
+(`G73`) to four diameters, and the full-retract peck (`G83`) past that.
+Choose **Deep peck (full retract)** to get `G83` on any hole, for example
+in a gummy material that packs chips.
+
 A cross drill can use a reduced-fidelity model when its mesh error leaves
 a positive verification tolerance. CamCraft increases the required
 stand-off, entry, reach and holder clearance to account for that error.

