@@ -116,3 +116,21 @@ fn a_cross_hole_reads_its_depth_from_the_mouth_and_takes_deep() {
     let t = cross_drill(&radial(&tool, &holes, CycleChoice::Deep)).expect("drills");
     assert_eq!(plunges(&t), 5, "full retracts of 2 mm steps from the standoff: -1, -3, -5, -7, -8");
 }
+
+/// The review case: the depth in material picks the Auto cycle, but the
+/// pecks still run from the R standoff. A far standoff is refused by the
+/// peck budget, never looped over: 30000 mm gives 10,000 pecks, and
+/// 1e20 is a step that cannot move `t`. This holds for an explicit Peck
+/// and for the Peck that Auto chooses.
+#[test]
+fn a_far_radial_standoff_is_refused_by_the_peck_budget() {
+    let tool = drill_tool(2.0);
+    let holes = [cross_hole(-8.0)];
+    for cycle in [CycleChoice::Peck, CycleChoice::Auto, CycleChoice::Deep] {
+        for r_d in [30_000.0, 1e20] {
+            let p = CrossParams { r_d, ..radial(&tool, &holes, cycle) };
+            let e = cross_drill(&p).expect_err("a far standoff is refused");
+            assert!(e.to_string().contains("peck plan unusable"), "{cycle:?} at {r_d}: {e}");
+        }
+    }
+}

From 708d6e7055c35ba020337bda04f2d8dcbc530770 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:07:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(app): Auto's new drill cycle makes old caches stale

Auto now chooses the drill cycle from the depth in material (#2443),
but the drill parameter digest does not change. A cache saved on main
would read current and post the old cycle. By the #3704 rule the PR
that changes generator output bumps GENERATOR_OUTPUT_VERSION: it goes
from 1 to 2, so every cache saved under 1 reads Stale once and clears
on regenerate.

The committed catalog caches are rebuilt (cargo xtask catalog; no .nc
moved), and the pinned stamps of deburr_cache_stamp and wire_stamp are
captured again, as #3704 did.

Pinned by stamp::tests::
a_drill_cache_saved_before_the_2443_bump_reads_stale_and_does_not_post
(the catalog first-part Drill1 with a pre-bump stamp reads Stale, the
post refuses it by name, and once generated again it posts G73).

Refs #2443

